{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38240 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound (6aR,9R)-N-[(1S,2S,4R,7S)-2-hydroxy-5-oxo-4,7-di(propan-2-yl)-3-oxa-6,9-diazatricyclo[7.3.0.02,6]dodecan-4-yl]-7-methyl-6,6a,8,9-tetrahydro-4H-indolo[4,3-fg]quinoline-9-carboxamide exerts its effect on U373 MG cells. The compound is identified as a target for multiple enzymes, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which are both targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This suggests that the compound may act through a shared pathway involving the enzyme inhibition of these targets, which in turn may affect U373 MG cells. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the inhibition of enzymes that are involved in cellular processes critical for the survival and proliferation of U373 MG, a cell line often associated with cancer. The integration of multiple targets and their shared pathway supports the hypothesis that the compound may exert its effects through a mechanism involving enzyme inhibition, which is a well-documented mode of action in drug-target relationships.",
